From cda4d663b5b41e9b9bd7cf802268f1455051c4d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poco-X3-Pro-ghost-touch-fix contributors
 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:53:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: Switch NT36xxx touch firmware blobs to
 V12.5.5.0.RJUIDXM prod

The j20s (POCO X3 Pro / vayu) Novatek NT36672C is a no-flash touch IC:
these blobs are embedded in the kernel image and uploaded to the
controller on every boot, so the firmware loaded by the kernel directly
controls the touch IC and can therefore affect ghost-touch behaviour.
The firmware version currently in this tree is associated with random
ghost touches (phantom taps, scrolling, text selection) on a subset of
panels.

These blobs, labeled V12.5.5.0.RJUIDXM prod by the community tree that
introduced them, ship as the default j20s firmware in several vayu
community kernels and have been used to address the widely reported
ghost touch issue. Both panel variants are covered: fw01 (DT config
"nvt+tianma", TP vendor 0x46) and fw02 ("nvt+csot", 0x53). The No
Gravity kernel carries a fw01 build that is identical apart from 33
bytes of version/tuning fields; rebuilding LineageOS with those NGK
blobs was publicly reported to eliminate ghost touches (LineageOS 22.2
XDA thread, posts #1366/#1368).

Decoded firmware sha256:
  fw01: 610f3521e3fb384f11f43d49a71e9eb9e8990f0b004d0a7532ec749e2b866334
  fw02: 7392a835cca1296f552c613a9678722a5312403950018ff1af27f4adc704cb7e

Historical ghost touch reports (former LineageOS GitLab issue tracker):
  https://gitlab.com/LineageOS/issues/android/-/issues/4309
  https://gitlab.com/LineageOS/issues/android/-/issues/5679
---
 firmware/j20s_novatek_ts_fw01.bin.ihex | 10036 +++++++++++------------
 firmware/j20s_novatek_ts_fw02.bin.ihex | 10020 +++++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 10028 insertions(+), 10028 deletions(-)

